{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532801-what-if-the-requiem-replace-the-masquerade-in-the-world-of-darkness","id":1532801,"title":"What if the Requiem replace the Masquerade in the World of Darkness?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-18T00:54:10-07:00","id":1532801,"title":"What if the Requiem replace the Masquerade in the World of Darkness?","content":"Lifted directly from Chronicle of Darkness. <br /> <br /> Instead of being a divergent evolution, vampire are convergent with no clear progeniter. They would also have no Trait taint since they're not from World of Darkness but Werewolf would sense something similiar. Vampire would be more unified, and less horrible to humanity. The Strix would have a realm to there own somewhere in the Low Umbra or the Deep Umbra. Blood Bond would be less common, and Ghoul would be treated better. They aren't affected by the Consensus reality but are affected by supernatural ability created from Consensus reality. They have a lot of advantage even before discipline and they also suffer less from the sun and fire is just more effective to vampire.<br /> <br /> What kind of relationship would they have with the other splat? I especially curious how they would deal with the kue-jin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T17:56:43-07:00","id":1532830,"title":"","content":"Perhaps vampires would exert less political control over mortal governments and mortal organizations? In general, Requiem vampires seemed to be less concerned with maintaining the Masquerade, though it is difficult to tell the extent to which that is due to their nature and not just the setting. Furthermore, Requiem vampires seem more solitary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T21:36:22-07:00","id":1532833,"title":"","content":"Why do you think they're more solitary? If anything they're even more social, while they might not have a single unified goverment like the Camarilla, Sabbat, or Anarch, but they have clan, covenant, and bloodline all of which have some sort of organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T00:15:21-07:00","id":1532836,"title":"","content":"\u0130 agree that Requiem - especially 2e - vampires are more solitary.<br /> First, Requiem 2e disciplines are very strong and allow a vampire to function alone for feeding and safety quite easily.<br /> Second, elders are more prone to torpor because they can't set up a worldwide scheme to ensure fresh vampire blood. Cities being - from the vampire point of view - more isolated means organisation is mostly local. There are covenants, sure, but they're not as centrally managed as the Camarilla or Sabbat, which have a more or less known &quot;board of directors&quot; that pulls the strings across the globe. Therefore, new vampires have less pressure to stick together to resist elders, and this makes them at least a bit more solitary, even if they can and do still team up for company, comfort (easier feeding and daytime protection by pooling resources and talents), and protection against other supernatural creatures, as well as socialising and to learn more about their condition and its management... leading to the Covenants.<br /> Masquerade-wise, Requiem vampires (\u0130'm always thinking 2e, \u0130 practically forgot the first edition) do have it, but it's obviously not as strictly enforced as it is in VtM, and it varies (like everything) from city to city.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T03:53:24-07:00","id":1532840,"title":"","content":"How would their relationship with the other splat be different from the Masquerade Vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T05:38:15-07:00","id":1532847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532801-what-if-the-requiem-replace-the-masquerade-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=1532840#post1532840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would their relationship with the other splat be different from the Masquerade Vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u0130 think it depends on many things, especially ST decisions since Requiem is not as lore-defined as Masquerade. For starters, there is no history of their relationship with other splats, unlike the meta of VtM.<br /> <br /> Kuei-jin: they sound a bit like a possible variation of the standard Requiem vampire - something already explored to some extent in Requiem manuals - but they also have too many unique mechanics and powers to be simply written as an unusual vampire type. The relation might be similar to that of VtM: both groups sense they have something in common, but they are also different. However, Requiem vampires do not assume all vampires have one progenitor or similar origin, so they will accept an alternative narrative for their origin and related differences.<br /> <br /> Mummies: the whole plot of the fight against Set and Apophis would be lost, as Requiem Set is something different and mainly relevant to some Mekhet cults. \u0130t's basically like a blank slate. ST can do what he want here.<br /> <br /> Werewolves: Requiem vampires would attract banes just like masquerade vampires, because of the feeding etc. or maybe a little less because there are no roads of enlightenment (but Humanity isn't exactly &quot;moral&quot;). \u0130n time, they would be antagonists anyway, just maybe less relevant to the Garou than other foes - which is already the case with VtM vampires.<br /> <br /> Mages: the main difference is that having multiple origins for the clans opens the way for some clans or bloodlines to have extra links to mages, but then it risks becoming &quot;Tremere and Nagaraja: part 2&quot;<br /> <br /> can't really of the others right now, but in short: the main change isn't the mechanics, but the lore. The absence of VtM lore is what would bring the biggest changes in the relationships.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T06:19:19-07:00","id":1532849,"title":"","content":"Would the Strix kill Bane?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T06:24:17-07:00","id":1532850,"title":"","content":"I'd stop playing.<br /> <br /> Same as before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T07:13:49-07:00","id":1532854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532801-what-if-the-requiem-replace-the-masquerade-in-the-world-of-darkness#post1532801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lifted directly from Chronicle of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Instead of being a divergent evolution, vampire are convergent with no clear progeniter. They would also have no Trait taint since they're not from World of Darkness</div> </div> </div> </div>Not how that works, chief.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but Werewolf would sense something similiar. </div> </div> </div>Yes, because they do shitty things to people, constantly, and bend over backward to justify it to themselves so that they can continue doing it. The end sum of all of the blood-drinking, empty sensation, and desperate search to avoid being hollowed out inside is what attracts banes and what not, regardless of where they were from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampire would be more unified, and less horrible to humanity. The Strix would have a realm to there own somewhere in the Low Umbra or the Deep Umbra. Blood Bond would be less common, and Ghoul would be treated better. They aren't affected by the Consensus reality but are affected by supernatural ability created from Consensus reality. They have a lot of advantage even before discipline and they also suffer less from the sun and fire is just more effective to vampire.<br /> <br /> What kind of relationship would they have with the other splat? I especially curious how they would deal with the kue-jin. </div> </div> </div>Pretty much none of the &quot;no one likes vampires&quot; will change, because the Kindred of Requiem are still not particularly pleasant company.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T07:33:16-07:00","id":1532855,"title":"","content":"\u0130 forgot an important bit: Requiem vampires have few active elders, for reasons \u0130 mentioned earlier. This makes vampires as a species weaker, even if neonates have stronger disciplines. \u0130n VtM elders have an important function in fortifying vampire society against other supernaturals, both as leaders and as powerhouses. Requiem vampires lack this particular advantage. WtA werewolves would find it quite easy to drive vampires to extinction, except maybe the Mekhet because of Obfuscate <i>depending on the rules used for that vs Werewolf gifts and advantages.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","user":"Hermeticus","date":".  corrected WtF into WtA 03-20-2024, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T08:00:05-07:00","id":1532857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532801-what-if-the-requiem-replace-the-masquerade-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=1532855#post1532855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WtF werewolves would find it quite easy to drive vampires to extinction, except maybe the Mekhet because of Obfuscate <i>depending on the rules used for that vs Werewolf gifts and advantages.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>You mean werewolf the apocalypse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T02:13:08-07:00","id":1532891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532801-what-if-the-requiem-replace-the-masquerade-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=1532857#post1532857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean werewolf the apocalypse?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, \u0130 do. \u0130t was a typo, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T17:09:23-07:00","id":1532928,"title":"","content":"We kinda tried that; just because, some players didn't like NWoD, so we tried a hybrid; we got rid of generation, replaced it with Blood-Potency. Cain was a myth, but the bases of vampire-beliefs. Players just like OWoD rules, but some elements of Requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T05:02:42-07:00","id":1533117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532801-what-if-the-requiem-replace-the-masquerade-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=1532840#post1532840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would their relationship with the other splat be different from the Masquerade Vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much doubt that this would work as a general rule, to justify itself the WOD made each splat avoid interacting with others for reasons, generally very well justified paranoia. Even if they tried to establish some relationship with other supernaturals they would be treated with great caution if not violently. I think at most one mage or another would try something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-10T09:39:47-07:00","id":1535414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532801-what-if-the-requiem-replace-the-masquerade-in-the-world-of-darkness#post1532801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lifted directly from Chronicle of Darkness.<br /> ...<br /> they're not from World of Darkness</div> </div> </div> </div>I think those are far more important points in your take of the question than anything else.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bHow those creatures come to the cWoD and how their first interactions with each splat happen are far more defining of those new relationships than anything else.<br /> <br /> Even if we assume they had always been there, defining previous interactions would be relevant, but as you stated the question it is even more so.<br /> <br /> Now I'm thinking about a large meteor carrying stranded vampires inside...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T17:47:12-07:00","id":1535697,"title":"","content":"V5. You'd get V5. The whole shitshow these past five-ish years was been about Paradox trying and failing to merge certain elements of Requiem (and CofD as a whole) with Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T21:35:51-07:00","id":1536920,"title":"","content":"It would be a good thing, but it won't happen. What's happened with The Masquerade is how religions are created. It's fiction, but there's something about human nature that allows fiction to become popular belief, and then cannon. In Mage terms, &quot;The Consensus.&quot;<br /> <br /> Requiem attempted to fix the obvious flaws of Masquerade. The strict heirarchy, the cemented Judeo-Christian foundation. In my opinion, it's a better system for the Game Master. They can create their own flavor of the &quot;Metafiction.&quot; But apparently, the people who think Lucita, Beckett, and Anatole are real don't like it. The &quot;Metafiction&quot; that I always though was very poor writing, and I always ignored. But like they say, opinons are like a-holes. Everybody has one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}